    "definitions": {
      "short": "properly, a (peremptory) terminus , i.e. (by implication) duration , in the sense of advance or perpetuity (substantially as a noun, either with or without a preposition)",
      "usage": "eternity, ever(-lasting, -more), old, perpetually, world without end.",
      "full": "H5703. ad I. עַד and וָעֶ֑ד (so always) noun masculine perpetuity (= advancing time, compare Assyrian adû, time at the present times ); — 1 of past time: עַר מִנִּי Job 20:4 ; עד הררי Hab 3:6 ancient mountains (compare עולם 1 ). **so Gen 49:26 (read עַד הַרְרֵי for עַד הוֺרַ֔י ). 2 of future time , לָעַד (usually לָעַ֑ד ) for ever: a. during lifetime, of king Psa 21:7 ; Prov 29:14 ; of others Psa 9:19 ; 22:27 ; Psalm 61:9; Prov 12:19 . b. of things , יֵחָֽצֵב֑וּן בַּצּוּר לָעַד Job 19:24 . c. of continuous existence , of nations, עַד גְּבֶרֶת (of Babylon, compare עולם 2c ) Isa 47:7 (yet see III. עַד II 3 ); anger , לעד Amos 1:11 ; elsewhere עַד עֲדֵי Psa 83:18 ; 92:8 ; Isa 26:4 ; 65:18 . d. of divine existence , עַד שֹׁכֵן Isa 57:15 ; attributes, לָעַד Psa 111:3 ; 111:10 ; 112:3 ; 112:9 ; residence in Zion, עַד עֲדֵי 132:14 ; law of God לָעַד 19:10 ; promise as to dynasty of David, לָעד 89:30 ; עַד עֲדֵי 132:12 ; inheritance of land, לָעַד 37:29 ; continuous relations between God and his people 1Chr 28:9 ; Isa 64:8 ; Micah 7:18 לעד . e. phrases (see עולם 2m ): וָעֶ֑ד (לְ)וְֺלָם Psa 9:6 ; 10:16 ; 21:5 ; 45:7 ; Psalm 45:18; Psalm 48:15; Psalm 52:10; 104:5 ; 119:44 ; 145:1 ; 145:2 ; 145:21 ; Exod 15:18 ; Micah 4:5 ; Dan 12:3 ; לְעוֺלָם לָעַד Psa 111:8 ; 148:6 ; עַד עַדעֿוֺלְמֵי Isa 45:17 . &#8212; 30:8 read ( עַדעֿוֺלָם ) לְעֵד for a witness ᵑ7 ᵑ9 ᵑ6 Ges Ew Di Che Du) for לָעַד ᵑ0 .",
